        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12532333/comment/13155493",
          "id": "13155493",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael D\u00fcrig",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Bucharest"
          },
          "body": "On a second though removing the comperator field from the Key class might have some subtle side effects. The patch might break things in the situation where different ValueIndex instances should go into the cache for the same field and same prefix but a for a different FieldComparator implementation: despite different, both ValueIndex instances end up at the same cache slot.\n\nTo be on the safe side I think the comperator should thus 'somehow' stay in the Key class. One solution might be to use a WeakReference instead the comperator instance itself. Another (a bit hacky) solution might be to use the comepator's hashCode instead of the comperator instance itself.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael D\u00fcrig",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Bucharest"
          },
          "created": "2011-11-22T22:20:56.181+0000",
          "updated": "2011-11-22T22:20:56.181+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12532333/comment/13155528",
          "id": "13155528",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "> The patch might break things in the situation where different ValueIndex instances should go into the cache for the same field and same prefix but a for a different FieldComparator implementation: despite different, both ValueIndex instances end up at the same cache slot.\n\nAgreed, what I cannot understand is the relation between the ValueIndex and the provided field comparator implementation. To me they are 2 different things. Just look at how the ValueIndex cache is being build.\nSo I'm not sure if them \"ending up at the same cache slot\" is actually a bad thing :)\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2011-11-22T22:47:47.303+0000",
          "updated": "2011-11-22T22:47:47.303+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12532333/comment/13155538",
          "id": "13155538",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
